From cfda5f5f3d84d6c24d941ef22880dfa7d5eb1974 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick Kennedy <nick@nick-kennedy.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 08:30:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: fix stitch_passes GPU timeouts in Alyx

Metal command allocators of command buffers that take part in a stitched
render pass are no longer returned to the pool when recording ends.
They are held until the commit containing them completes and then go to
a device-wide list that new command buffers draw from. Reusing them
early let later recordings append to an allocator whose suspended render
encoder Metal had not yet merged, which caused intermittent
MTL_COMMAND_QUEUE_ERROR_TIMEOUT in Alyx; a 30 ms sleep after each
stitched commit also hid it.

Submission now gathers each chain of suspended and resumed command
buffers before committing. A chain that breaks the stitching rules, for
example a barrier split inside a middle segment, or one left open at
the end of a submission, is re-recorded without stitching and committed
in submission order. Re-recorded command buffers in a split final
segment are released only after both of their commits complete.
Stitching statistics are reported through KK_ENCODER_STATS.

AI-written commit text (biblioklept).

